thout knowing White’s response.\n\nOr ...Qd8-e7, solid.\n\nBut **...d7-d5** is the most principled central counterblow.\n\nReason: Playing d7-d5 immediately challenges White’s central presence (knight on e5), opens lines for Black’s pieces (queen and bishop), and seizes space in the center, improving overall activity and development prospects.\n\nAnswer: P: d7-d5'}
