cking development or preparing ...Nf6.\n\nHowever, the most promising move appears to be **P: g7-g5**, because:\n- It activates the h8-rook indirectly.\n- It creates immediate threats against White’s kingside, especially if White hasn’t completed safe development.\n- It prevents White from easily playing g2-g4 to gain space later.\n- The pawn push can support future ...g4 ideas, trapping pieces like the Nf1 (though not present yet) or disrupting White’s coordination.\n\nReason:  \nPushing **g7-g5** begins active counterplay on the kingside, where White has minimal presence. It increases dynamic chances and avoids passive development. Given that White may have ambitions in the center, creating imbalances now while maintaining flexibility elsewhere is optimal.\n\nAnswer: P: g7-g5"}
